00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:11.843
- Oh, that's cool.

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:13.920
- And there were a lot of fans.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.270
- And it was in Britain, right?

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.550
And that's where you actually
shot the movie, right?

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.383
- Part of it, yeah.

00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:20.820
It was all in studio there
and it was also in Morocco.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.440
But it was nice to go back

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.510
and say, "Hey, thanks for
making such a great movie."

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.850
- Yeah 'cause there's a couple.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.380
So speaking of "The Mummy,"

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.735
is this the one that you almost died?

00:02:30.735 --> 00:02:33.450
- Nearly... well, I was
choked out accidentally.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.470
There's a hanging sequence.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.330
- I know what you're
talking about, the sequence.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.580
I didn't know that that actually happened.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.420
- Well, I don't remember too.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.253
Oh gosh, yeah.

00:02:40.253 --> 00:02:42.187
- They tightened it so much that you-

00:02:42.187 --> 00:02:43.680
(Brendan clears throat)

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.073
Like, what happened?

00:02:45.073 --> 00:02:48.360
- I was standing on my
toes like this with a rope

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.880
and you only got so far to go.
- Yeah.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.817
And Steve ran over and he said,

00:02:51.817 --> 00:02:55.140
"Hey, it doesn't really
look like you're choking.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:55.973
Can you...

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:57.953
sell it?"

00:02:57.953 --> 00:02:59.580
And I'm like, all right, fine.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.230
So I thought, one more take, man.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.290
And the camera swooped around
and I went up on the toes

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.410
and the guy holding the rope above me,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.270
he pulled it up a little higher
and I was stuck on my toes.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.310
I had nowhere to go, but down.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.900
And so he was pulling
up and I was going down.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:16.170
And then the next thing I
knew, my elbow was in my ear.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.810
The world was sideways and
there was gravel in my teeth.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.760
And everyone was really quiet.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.760
And there was a stunt
guy from the coordinator

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.114
was there and he was
going (hands clapping),

00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:26.589
(softly) "Brendan"

00:03:26.589 --> 00:03:28.500
(hands clapping) "Brendan, wake up."

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.577
And I'm like, "Oh, what, what happened?"

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.467
"Congratulations. You're in the club."

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:35.695
"Same thing happened to Mel
Gibson on 'Braveheart.'"

00:03:35.695 --> 00:03:37.260
- Oh, my god.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.378
- Thanks, I think.

00:03:39.378 --> 00:03:41.220
I wanna go home!

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.110
- I love that he said Mel
Gibson in "Braveheart."

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.607
Was he like accidentally gutted?

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:46.512
- I think he was, yes.

00:03:46.512 --> 00:03:49.440
Off to a blazing start
in this movie so far.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.400
- Oh, my gosh.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.270
That's scary.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.477
I would've been like,

00:03:52.477 --> 00:03:53.820
"The acting is fine,

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.410
I'm not choking for you."

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.460
So wait, I love this about you

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.770
because I'm not good at taking photographs

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.821
but you're into photography
and you're so amazing at it.

00:04:00.821 --> 00:04:01.654
- Oh, thanks.

00:04:01.654 --> 00:04:02.487
- Yeah, you have a great eye.

00:04:02.487 --> 00:04:03.630
I got to see some of your work

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.370
and I wanna show everyone that.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.701
But how did you get into it?

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.240
- I picked up a camera.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.073
- Don't do that.

00:04:10.073 --> 00:04:11.120
And you just were amazing at it.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.230
- It was one of those
old Polaroid cameras,

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.170
the accordion ones and they sell packfilm.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.220
Prolifically in the 90s.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.260
And I wanted some instant gratification

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.090
and they gave these
really beautiful little

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.140
black and white images.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.080
No negative and one-of-a-kind
kind of feelings.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.130
That's how I started.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:26.970
- I love that.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.803
I love a polar-

00:04:27.803 --> 00:04:29.550
I own like three different kinds.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.720
I love Polaroids.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.070
Well, okay, here's one.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.410
So this photo, can you
tell us about this one?

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.243
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:35.243 --> 00:04:37.590
I shot a film called "The Quiet American"

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.483
in Vietnam in 2001.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:45.980
The story is that of an
American who goes to Vietnam

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.840
bringing foreign policy and aid.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.070
And it's a controversial film

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:55.560
for its criticism of
American foreign policy,

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.393
blah, blah, blah.

00:04:56.393 --> 00:04:59.193
But that meant that we
were the first production,

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.573
Western production in
Vietnam to shoot a film-

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.273
- Since?
- in forever.

00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:06.480
And, that was in 2001.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.280
But that meant because
it's a communist country

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.010
that the cops were always
following us around the place.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.410
So we were infiltrated by Hanoi...

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.700
and these were the cops.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.810
And they were always following us around

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.400
until one day I just went, "Hey, hi!"

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.740
And they just walked up and
started taking pictures.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.963
So we end up making friends with them.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.321
They're really nice guys, you know?

00:05:25.321 --> 00:05:26.730
- I love the photo that you took,

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.950
even the ones where you could
just see the eyes in the back.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.360
It's like each one has a story

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.560
that they're telling like with their eyes.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.393
I love it.

00:05:32.393 --> 00:05:33.226
It's really cool.

00:05:33.226 --> 00:05:34.059
Yeah, nice shot.

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:35.280
Nice eye, I don't have that.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.113
I'm so jealous.

00:05:36.113 --> 00:05:37.667
- Just bring a camera with you.

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:38.500
It helps.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.780
- I bring the camera, Brendan.

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.354
And it doesn't go out that way.

00:05:41.354 --> 00:05:42.690
- Oh, If you look really closely.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.280
That's Michael Caine.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.540
And he was my scene
partner in the film also.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.500
And that's a bunker.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.510
There was a scene where
we were getting shelled

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.850
and it was very muddy and dug out.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.660
And to keep myself from feeling
like I was going bonkers,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.100
I started taking pictures of stuff.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.630
And so anyway, that's Michael.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.463
- Yeah.

00:06:01.463 --> 00:06:03.300
- I think it's good to
have something to do

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.030
that's outside of your job, you know.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:09.960
And capturing images is something
that is important to me.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.070
- I quilt.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:11.903
- Good for you.

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:13.105
- Not good at it, but I love doing it.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:14.160
- Doesn't matter.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.500
I'm an amateur enthusiast
with the camera anyway.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.174
- I think it's awesome.

00:06:18.174 --> 00:06:20.760
So since you were here a couple months ago

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.290
you got an Oscar nomination.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:23.636
We knew it was gonna happen.

00:06:23.636 --> 00:06:24.469
(audience cheering)

00:06:24.469 --> 00:06:27.810
Everyone knew it was gonna happen.

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.920
How did you find out?

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.240
That's really cool news.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.060
- Watching the broadcast at home.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.180
In the morning, there was a
knock at the door of my bedroom

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.620
and my kids were there with balloons

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.630
and they had a Carvel ice cream cake.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.040
- Oh my god, I will cry right now.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.270
That's so sweet.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.683
- It was Fudgie the Whale.

00:06:44.848 --> 00:06:47.820
- Aw. Ice cream cakes are good.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.653
- Oh, yes.

00:06:48.653 --> 00:06:50.520
- Yeah.
- Enjoyed that one.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.380
And now it's a core memory of mine.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.667
- I love that.

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.530
Are you getting prepared for a speech?

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:58.260
Do you prepare speeches
or are you superstitious?

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.470
- Fail to prepare, prepare to fail.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.513
- Oh, you know what, I'm the first one.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:05.610
- I'm gonna put something in mind,

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.813
keep it behind glass with
a little hammer on it,

00:07:08.813 --> 00:07:11.130
in case of emergency, break,

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.967
and then I'll be able to
thank all those people

00:07:12.967 --> 00:07:14.700
that helped get me where I need to be.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.160
- Speaking of words, you got
an amazing bowling trophy

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.780
that we replenished for you.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:21.030
So has it found a really
cool place in your home?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.670
- Yeah, it's actually in the
offices of A24 right now.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:24.780
- Okay, perfect.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:28.140
I just think it should go
right next to your Oscar.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.280
- I'll have them send it on.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.180
- I want you to put it right
next to the Oscar 'cause hmm.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.640
So, this was interesting.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.920
You worked with a dance
instructor for the role.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.320
- Yeah, Beth Lewis is a dance instructor

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.610
who danced in Pilobolus company

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.260
for like seven or eight years.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.480
Wonderful knowledge of the human body.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.760
And because Charlie is created

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.403
with prosthetic makeup and appliances,

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:56.900
it was a cumbersome
costume, appropriately.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:01.410
And to drive home the reality

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.570
of who he is and what it's
like to live with that

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.550
she would be in strict observation

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:08.520
of keeping a momentum to his every motion,

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.520
to teaching me how to
walk, observing gestures.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:19.560
And it was very important
that we have such specificity

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.140
because up until now,

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:25.320
the use of this costuming
in films and makeup

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.496
has always been, to my mind,

00:08:27.496 --> 00:08:32.496
in service of a mean joke
or to vilify a character.

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.250
And I don't think we need
to do that any longer.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.380
So the rule with the
creation of him was that

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:43.320
the makeup should obey the
laws of physics and gravity.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.180
Whereas before it had been, you know,

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:49.080
a fairly fit actor in a
costume that's a silhouette

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.760
that's filled with cotton
batting and you know,

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.703
your mind just goes, I'll
pretend I believe that,

00:08:52.703 --> 00:08:54.660
but you really don't.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.250
With this, it's seamless.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.240
It had to be.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.070
- It would change your
gait, like your walk,

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.060
everything about it.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:00.893
- Everything.

00:09:00.893 --> 00:09:04.530
And that was born of
paying close attention

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.410
to documentary footage,
to speaking to members

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.243
of the Obesity Action Coalition,

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:13.410
and observing all of the sensitivities.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:17.160
And then most importantly, to my mind,

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.580
just forget about all the
gear that I was wearing

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.440
and just play the scenes.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.790
Connect with my daughter.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.730
Connect with Hong Chau
who's also nominated

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.800
for Best Supporting Actress in her role.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.290
- That's awesome for you to mention that.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.350
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.720
We have some footage of
you getting into character,

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.040
which is crazy.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:35.873
- Oh, look at that.

00:09:35.873 --> 00:09:38.763
- I mean, how long does this take?

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:41.010
- That morning, four hours.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.570
- Oh, my god.
- Four hours and change.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:43.950
So we would get there very early

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.570
but don't feel sad for me

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:49.110
because Adrien Moreau had
to get there before me

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.850
and he was always the last boots to leave

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:51.683
at the end of the day.

00:09:51.683 --> 00:09:52.950
Oh, there I am sleeping.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:54.720
Yes, it's probably like about six o'clock

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:55.830
in the morning now.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:56.663
They woke me up.

00:09:56.663 --> 00:09:58.680
Someone gave me a smoothie.
- Someone gimme a smoothie.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.960
It's like so quick. (laughs)

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.190
Oh, my gosh.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:05.010
Okay, so let's see how all
of that work came together.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.390
Here's Brendan Fraser

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.847
in his Oscar-nominated
role in "The Whale."

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:14.140
- I need to know that she's
just gonna have a decent life

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.490
where she cares about people

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.570
and other people care about her

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.013
and she's gonna be okay.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.127
- I need to go.

00:10:25.127 --> 00:10:26.145
- She doesn't-
- I have to go.

00:10:26.145 --> 00:10:27.728
- have anyone else.

00:10:28.716 --> 00:10:32.774
I need to know that I
have done one day right

00:10:32.774 --> 00:10:35.483
with my life.

00:10:35.483 --> 00:10:40.483
- I can't...
(audience applauds)

00:10:40.925 --> 00:10:42.390
What?

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:45.120
Like, I've seen it and it still gets me.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.920
That's... okay.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.090
I just need a minute.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:48.930
Look-

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.100
I'll get all this makeup on.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.571
This isn't real.

00:10:51.571 --> 00:10:53.070
(laughs)

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:54.180
You're so kind.
- I gotta prepare.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.023
Q&amp;A Sessions and question, answers.

00:10:56.023 --> 00:10:58.440
After-screenings of this,

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.240
people feel that they have
really gone through something

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:03.960
- It doesn't even matter
how much you see it.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.310
It's so good.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:08.670
Brendan, it's so believable, it hurts.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:09.547
It's fine.

00:11:09.547 --> 00:11:13.170
"The Whale" is in theaters
and on demand now.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.580
Go see it.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.203
Especially feel like a good cry.

